      "text": "Below is a practical shortlist for small consulting firms. Prices are approximate US list prices with annual billing; G2 ratings are rounded and change over time.\n\n| CRM | G2 rating* | Starting price | Consulting-relevant features | Main drawback |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| **Capsule CRM** | **4.7/5** | Free plan; paid from **~$18/user/mo** | Simple contact and opportunity management, project boards, task \u201ctracks,\u201d Gmail/Microsoft 365 and accounting integrations | Less sophisticated reporting and automation |\n| **monday CRM** | **4.6/5** | **~$12/user/mo**, usually 3-seat minimum | Highly customizable pipelines, automations, dashboards, email tracking and easy project-delivery handoff | Costs rise with automation needs; setup can take time |\n| **Freshsales** | **4.5/5** | Free plan; paid from **~$9/user/mo** | Built-in email and phone, lead scoring, sequences, workflows and multiple pipelines | Advanced AI and reporting require higher tiers |\n| **Copper** | **4.5/5** | From **~$9\u2013$12/user/mo** | Excellent Google Workspace integration, relationship tracking, pipelines, email sync and task management | Best value mainly for Google-centric firms |\n| **HubSpot Sales Hub** | **4.4/5** | Strong free plan; Starter from **~$15/user/mo** | CRM, meeting scheduler, email templates/tracking, quotes, marketing and service tools | Professional tiers become expensive quickly |\n| **Pipedrive** | **4.3/5** | From **~$14/user/mo** | Excellent visual pipeline, activity reminders, email sync, workflow automation, forecasting and proposal integrations | Limited project management; some core tools require higher plans/add-ons |\n| **Insightly CRM** | **4.2/5** | From **~$29/user/mo** | Relationship mapping, pipeline-to-project conversion, milestones, workflow automation and Gmail/Microsoft integration | Higher entry price and less intuitive interface |\n| **Zoho CRM** | **4.1/5** | Free for 3 users; paid from **~$14/user/mo** | Deep customization, workflow rules, Blueprint processes, analytics and broad Zoho finance/project integration | Configuration and interface can feel complex |\n\n### Best choices by consulting-firm need\n\n- **Best overall simplicity:** Capsule  \n- **Best customizable CRM/project workflow:** monday CRM  \n- **Best value with automation:** Freshsales or Zoho CRM  \n- **Best for Google Workspace:** Copper  \n- **Best free CRM and future marketing expansion:** HubSpot  \n- **Best sales-pipeline experience:** Pipedrive  \n- **Best CRM-to-client-project handoff:** Insightly  \n\nFor most firms under ten people, I would shortlist **Capsule, Pipedrive and Freshsales**. Choose **HubSpot** if marketing is central, or **monday CRM** if client delivery workflows matter as much as sales.\n\n\\*Ratings are approximate G2 scores; pricing, packaging and ratings should be verified before purchase."
